093 - All Things Bright and Beautiful
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 93
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[G]All things bright and [Bm/F#]beautiful, [C/E]All creatures [Bm/D]great and small,
[C]All things wise and wonderful, The Lord [G]God made them all.
[Am]Each little flower [D]that opens, [D7]Each little bird [G]that sings;
[G]He made their glowing colors, [C/E]He made their [Bm/D]tiny wings.

Refrain:
[C]All things bright and beautiful
[Am]All creatures great [D]and small
[D7]All things wise and wonderful
[G]The Lord God made them all.

Verse 2:
[G]The purple-headed [C/E]mountain
[C]The river running [G]by
[Am]The sunset [D]and [D7]the morning
[G]That brighten [C/E]up the [Bm/D]sky.

Verse 3:
[G]The cold [Bm/F#]wind in [C/E]the winter
[C]The pleasant summer [G]sun
[Am]The ripe fruits [D]in [D7]the garden
[G]He made them, every [Bm/D]one.

Verse 4:
[G]He gave [Bm/F#]us eyes [C/E]to see [Bm/D]them
[C]And lips that we [G]might tell
[Am]How great is [D]God [D7]Almighty
[G]Who has made [C/E]all things [Bm/D]well.
